target: ipq95xx: enable the RTL8261N PHY driver

The SBE1V1K routes the 10G port through a Realtek RTL8261N; without
CONFIG_RTL8261N_PHY the dp1 link never comes up.  The driver itself is supplied
by build/kernel-overlay (18 files, SPDX GPL-2.0-only, provenance recorded in
docs/SOURCE_ASSEMBLY.md).

Apply from target/linux/feeds:  patch -p1 < 0001-...

--- a/ipq95xx/config-6.6
+++ b/ipq95xx/config-6.6
@@ -357,6 +357,7 @@
 CONFIG_CNSS2_QCA9574_SUPPORT=y
 CONFIG_QCA807X_PHY=y
 CONFIG_QCA808X_PHY=y
+CONFIG_RTL8261N_PHY=y
 # CONFIG_CNSS2_CALIBRATION_SUPPORT is not set
 # CONFIG_CNSS2_DEBUG is not set
 CONFIG_CNSS2_GENL=y
